The '''Transmatarrañya high speed rail line''' is a {{convert|409.58|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} inaugurated on 10 September 2009. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|360|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}, it connects the cities of [[Uxiu]], [[Guadalajara]] and [[San Marco]] in 1 hour and 15 minutes. The crosses the [[Matarrañya / Cañadapirén]] from Uxiu towards [[Guadalajara]] via tunnels of the [[New Railway Link]].

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service. 

